# Vercel Speed Insights Integration

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Vite + React project following the latest official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
**File**: `package.json`
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` (v2.0.0) as a dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new dependency and its 151 sub-packages

### 2. Speed Insights Integration
**File**: `src/main.tsx`
- Imported `injectSpeedInsights` from `@vercel/speed-insights`
- Called `injectSpeedInsights()` early in the application lifecycle, right after imports
- Added a descriptive comment explaining the initialization

## Implementation Details

### Framework-Specific Approach
This project uses Vite as the build tool with React. According to Vercel's Speed Insights documentation, for Vite applications, the recommended approach is to use the `injectSpeedInsights()` function in the main entry file rather than the React component approach.

The function was placed early in `main.tsx`, before any routing or conditional logic, to ensure Speed Insights tracks all user interactions across all application modes (including the special #puck and #flowbar hash routes).

### Verification
- ✅ TypeScript type checking passed (`npm run typecheck`)
- ✅ Production build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ Core test suites passed (audio, mix, tracking, insights, achievements)
- ✅ No new linting errors introduced
- ✅ Lock file updated correctly

## Next Steps for Deployment
Once deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights will automatically begin collecting Core Web Vitals metrics including:
- Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)
- First Input Delay (FID)
- Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)
- First Contentful Paint (FCP)
- Time to First Byte (TTFB)

Data will be visible in the Vercel dashboard under the "Speed Insights" tab after users visit the deployed application.

## Notes
- No configuration options were passed to `injectSpeedInsights()` - using defaults which is recommended for most use cases
- The integration is non-blocking and will not impact application startup performance
- Speed Insights respects user privacy and only collects anonymous performance metrics
